The '''Wand of Water''' (水の杖, ''Mizu no Tsue'') is a [[Spells|spell]] that shapes water into the shape of a large pen nib.

==Description==
[[File:Water Pen Seal Redraw.png|left|thumb|120px|<small>Wand of Water Seal Redraw (Ch. 24)</small>]]The Casting Seal contains a [[Sigils#Water|Sigil of Water]] within a [[Signs#Holding|Sign of Holding]]. Below the sigil is a [[Signs#Pointing|Sign of Pointing]] Above the sigil is one [[Signs#Dispersion|Sign of Dispersion]] pointing upwards and two [[Signs#Columns|Signs of Columns]] mirrored on either side of it.{{Ref|m|24|6-7}}{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 149}}

The [[Sigils#Water|Sigil of Water]] creates the water to be used for the spell. The [[Signs#Columns|Signs of Columns]] and [[Signs#Pointing|Pointing]] determine the shape that the water takes, with Columns defining the base of the 'nib' and Pointing causing the water to taper to a point. The 'wand' appears to hovers below the seal at an angle, which can be likely be attributed to the [[Signs#Dispersion|Sign of Dispersion]] causing spells to take effect outside of the confines of its ring. 

[[Conjuring Ink|Conjuring ink]] can be poured inside to saturate the water with ink.{{Ref|m|24|5}} It can be used to draw large Casting Seals on stone, sand, or likely any flat, expansive area.{{Ref|m|24|6-7}}{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 149}}{{Ref|m|24|11-12}}

==History==
[[Qifrey]] uses this spell while fending off [[the Ancients of Romonon]] in the [[Serpentback Cave]], using it to draw large Casting Seals in the ground,{{Ref|m|24|6-7}} one of which being a variation of [[Water Bolt]].{{Ref|m|24|11-12}}

==Notes==
